aquinas-second-way.logic.r2: argue/equivocates: P6 (S7): "first" is taken as absolutely first, uncaused efficient cause with nothing before it in P6 C and as first member of an ordered series of causes, i.e. the cause of the intermediate cause where first is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C3 (S7) does not follow (aquinas-second-way.logic.r2.sense1)
aquinas-second-way.logic.r2: argue/countermodel: C3 (S7): W = {w0, w1, w2, w3, w4, w5, w6, w7, w8, w9}; R = W × W; w0: first = T, first_2 = F, infinite = T, intermediate = T, ultimate = T; w1: first = F, first_2 = F, infinite = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w2: first = F, first_2 = F, infinite = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w3: first = F, first_2 = F, infinite = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w4: first = F, first_2 = F, infinite = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w5: first = F, first_2 = F, infinite = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w6: first = F, first_2 = F, infinite = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w7: first = F, first_2 = F, infinite = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w8: first = F, first_2 = F, infinite = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w9: first = F, first_2 = F, infinite = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F
aquinas-second-way.logic.r2: argue/countermodel: C (S8): W = {w0, w1, w2, w3, w4, w5, w6, w7, w8, w9}; R = W × W; w0: first = T, first_2 = F, intermediate = T, ultimate = T; w1: first = F, first_2 = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w2: first = F, first_2 = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w3: first = F, first_2 = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w4: first = F, first_2 = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w5: first = F, first_2 = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w6: first = F, first_2 = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w7: first = F, first_2 = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w8: first = F, first_2 = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F; w9: first = F, first_2 = F, intermediate = F, ultimate = F
